  </div>
  <p>The homology of <span data-field="object_name_27">{{ object_name_27 }}</span> is thus the stable homology of the mapping class group. In particular it is independent of <span data-field="parameter_n">{{ parameter_n }}</span>. The dependence on <span data-field="parameter_g">{{ parameter_g }}</span> is also completely understood and follows from the independence on <span data-field="parameter_n">{{ parameter_n }}</span>. Restricting the diffeomorphisms to a neighborhood of the punctures defines a map to <span data-field="group_name_5">{{ group_name_5 }}</span> which records the permutation of the punctures and the twisting around them. In stable homology this is a split surjection, see [BT]. Thus by the Künneth theorem, the following can be deduced.</p>
